<title>ITALY: Generali shares resume trade, up 1.08 pct.</title>
<headline>Generali shares resume trade, up 1.08 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Italian insurer Generali resumed trading on the Milan bourse up 1.08 percent at 33,250 lire after a delayed start due to the announcement of the sale of its stake in French insurer Axa, which is being bought by Axa itself.  </p>
<p>Earlier, the French insurer said it had bought Generali's 10.8 percent stake for 285 french francs per share representing 5.92 billion francs.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
